{
  "gang": "avaddon",
  "displayName": "Avaddon",
  "aliases": [],
  "status": "defunct",
  "activeSince": "2020",
  "lineage": "Shut down June 2021 and released decryption keys; ACSC noted TTP overlap with Ako and MedusaLocker",
  "summary": "Avaddon was a RaaS launched in June 2020 and shut down in June 2021, when it released its master keys. Affiliates relied heavily on mass malspam (including Phorpiex-distributed campaigns) carrying JavaScript downloaders with crude 'compromising photo' lures, which used PowerShell and BITSAdmin to fetch the payload. FBI and ACSC warned in May 2021 of an ongoing campaign that added DDoS threats to double extortion. The locker bypasses UAC via the CMSTPLUA COM interface, avoids CIS-language systems, persists through Run keys and scheduled tasks, stops database/AV services and destroys backups with wmic, wbadmin, bcdedit and vssadmin.",
  "uniqueTraits": [
    "Mass malspam with JavaScript (.jpg.js style) attachments and 'compromising photo' lures, partly via the Phorpiex botnet",
    "JScript downloader chaining PowerShell + BITSAdmin to retrieve the locker",
    "UAC bypass via the CMSTPLUA COM elevation interface",
    "GetUserDefaultLCID / keyboard-layout checks to avoid CIS-region victims",
    "Triple extortion: data leak site plus DDoS threats against non-payers (from Feb 2021)",
    "Wallpaper changed to point to 'Instruction <id>-readme.html'; .avdn extension"
  ],
  "insufficientReporting": false,
